### Create a new Klasse (CalendarSource)
# Replace {{baseUrl}} and {{token}} in your HTTP client environment (see api-tests.http)
# Provide the `name` and `ical_link` in the JSON body below.

POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/klassen
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "pbd2h24a",
  "ical_link": "https://intranet.bib.de/ical/d819a07653892b46b6e4d2765246b7ab"
}

### Example: create with variables
# You can also set variables at the top of the file or use your http-client env file:
# @baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000
# @token = <your-jwt-here>

### Notes
# - Endpoint expects JSON with `name` and `ical_link` (both required).
# - Successful response: 201 Created with JSON body (CreateKlasseResponse).
# - Use the script `scripts/get_token.ps1` to obtain a token for local Keycloak if needed.
#   Example PowerShell to get token and run this request in an HTTP client:
#     .\scripts\get_token.ps1; (copy token into http-client.private.env.json or set {{token}})

